## Plex agent coordination
This block is managed by the Plex installer; keep personal/project rules outside it.
Use the installed `plex` skill only when the user invokes Plex or explicitly requests coordinated multi-agent work. It is intended for complex tasks that benefit from specialist assignments; complexity alone does not activate it.
Otherwise, handle the task normally without loading a Plex coordinator. With Plex active, the root coordinates through native subagent calls for substantive task work; keep intake, integration, final checks and small mechanical actions local.
When Plex is active, delegate Plex-owned work only to exact `plex-<role>` identities in the checked `.plex/resolved.json` roles; other installed, built-in or stale agents are not part of the team. Follow the skill's dispatch and naming contract; workflow-owned leaves follow their workflow contract.
Use `plex-setup` to configure or refresh the team; configuration does not activate coordination.
Follow the project's instructions, required verification and human decision gates. BMad work requires its installed skills and runtime in the actual working project.
